# API Controllers (Node.js)

## Responsibilities

- Parse request (params, query, body); validate input (Zod or similar); call service; return status and body; handle errors via middleware or try/catch

## Conventions

- **Routes:** RESTful resources (GET /users, GET /users/:id, POST /users, etc.); use plural nouns; version in URL or header if needed
- **Status:** 200/201 for success; 204 for no content; 400 validation; 401 unauthenticated; 403 forbidden; 404 not found; 409 conflict; 500 server error
- **Body:** JSON; use RFC 7807 ProblemDetails for errors; consistent shape (e.g. { data } or { items, total })
- **Async:** Use async/await; forward errors to error middleware (do not swallow)

## Validation

- Validate at controller boundary (Zod schema, body/query/params); return 400 with details on failure; infer TypeScript type from schema

## Frameworks

- **Express:** Router, req/res, next; middleware for auth, validation
- **Fastify:** Schema-based validation; plugins
- **NestJS:** Controllers, DTOs, guards, pipes
- **Hono:** Lightweight, type-safe routing

## Conventions

- Thin controllers (delegate to services); consistent error handling; correlation ID in logs; no business logic in controller

## Anti-Patterns

- Business logic in controller; no validation; inconsistent status codes; leaking stack traces

